estors</b> on Investors.</p><p class="gd-p">How we make money is one slide with the seven revenue lines: our own cars, owners&#39; cars fully managed with coverage under our fleet policy, coverage under our fleet policy for owners who manage their own cars, Turo management, brokering partner fleets with the chauffeur service, detailing, and the body shop. The feature slides follow the platform as it is today. For renters: the rental walkthrough, CarmaCars Rewards, and Add to calendar and Apple Wallet. For owners: flat monthly pay per car as well as revenue share. For the team: one staff portal for every function, the training academy, the card reader and card payments, and insurer billing. Admin and automation: e-signatures everywhere with an audit trail, phone and browser alerts, and the live map. Growth: listing channels and feeds, the owner pipeline, and Facebook Marketplace kits. Their screens are real screens with fictional people; a feature with no screen shows how it works.</p><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>The deck shows no internal costs, fleet counts or staff pay. Every example is labelled as an illustration, with the forward-looking statements notice on every slide and in the PDF.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="the-investor-deck-the-updates-page" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The Updates page</h2><p class="gd-p">Investors have <b class="gd-ui">Updates</b> in their menu: every release of the platform, newest first, with the day it went live, a one-line summary and what it added for renters, owners, staff, partners, the website and reliability. Go to <b class="gd-ui">Investors</b> and press <b class="gd-ui">Updates (as investors see it)</b> to preview it. The text comes from the release notes written for investors with each release (<span class="gd-url">docs/releases</span>), never from the database: no fleet size, costs, names or incident details.</p></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('investor', 'quick-reference', 'reference', 'keeping-your-account-safe', '### Where things are

| Item | What it is for |
| --- | --- |
| **Home** | What needs you first, then each investment, returns, next payment |
| **Live sheets** | Your full schedule, the calculators and the Excel download |
| **Documents** | **Statements** (one per month; PDF, ZIP and CSV by year), **Documents to sign**, **Your files** (your agreement and schedules) |
| **Account** | Contact details, notices, transfers, two-step sign-in |

### Top tasks

1. *See what you earned:* **Documents** > **Statements**, then a month
2. *Keep a statement:* **Download PDF**
3. *A whole year:* **Documents** > **Statements**, then **Download a year**
4. *Paid monthly or reinvested:* **Send the notice**
5. *Change your bank account:* **Ask to change the bank account**
6. *Transfer an investment:* **Send the request**
7. *Protect your account:* **Set up two-step sign-in**

### If something goes wrong

| What you see | What to do |
| --- | --- |
| **A link says it expired** | Links in our emails work for 24 hours, once. Press **Send me a new link** on that page. |
| **"Error 1102" on a page** | A short limit on our web host. Reload the page. You are still signed in. |
| **"That email and password do not match an account."** | Check the address, or use **Set a new password** on the sign-in page. |
| **Asked for a 6-digit code** | Open your authenticator app. Lost your phone? Call us. |
